WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.760
Here's what you have ready,

2
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:03.280
and what you've chosen to

3
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:05.520
leave for later.

4
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.240
The summary below shows three

5
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.160
separate things:

6
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.560
your searchable history,

7
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.880
your personal guide, and where

8
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.520
your AI can use them.

9
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.760
Your history may already be

10
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.760
searchable even if you've done

11
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.240
little or no learning.

12
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.880
Meaning search is an extra

13
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.400
option.

14
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.480
Leaving it for later doesn't

15
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.040
remove the word-based search you've

16
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.120
prepared.

17
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.680
The personal-guide section shows how

18
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.360
much useful context has been

19
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.200
saved and how much reading

20
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.720
remains.

21
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.080
A small number of saved

22
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.040
details doesn't mean your other

23
00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.560
conversations are missing.

24
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.160
It means those details are

25
00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.600
what the assistant has drawn

26
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.440
out so far.

27
00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.000
The connection section shows where

28
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.920
your context is available.

29
00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.920
You'll also see the folder

30
00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.870
where it's stored.

31
00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:02.110
If that's on an external

32
00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:04.750
drive, keep it connected when

33
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.150
you need the history.

34
00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.150
You can add new exports

35
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.310
and correct mistakes as you

36
00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.750
go.

37
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.670
More learning happens when you

38
00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:18.430
ask, agree to continue, or

39
00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:21.870
set up a supported schedule.

40
00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:24.190
It doesn't run

41
00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:27.470
just because setup has finished.

42
00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:29.480
A good next step

43
00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.470
is one real question.

44
00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.870
For example, how have I

45
00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.950
approached this kind of decision

46
00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.710
before?

47
00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:41.870
Look at the sources, and

48
00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:44.830
correct anything that doesn't fit.

49
00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:45.950
Would you like to try

50
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.790
a question now, or finish

51
00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:48.870
here?
